{
  "rationale": "Model sensing and actuation separately. Use one sensor plant that emits the given obstacle/path events and one motion plant that admits the given motion commands. Then use compact specifications to: (i) bind clear sensing to forward-biased exploration with occasional random walk, (ii) force obstacle events into dedicated recovery states with one-shot directed turns, (iii) allow rare brief backward escape only for front blockage, and (iv) reserve full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front blockage. Action states self-loop on path_clear so intended open-loop pulses are not preempted, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception plant and motion plant; encode policy in specifications",
    "Bias clear-space behavior toward move_forward, with occasional random_walk but no steady turning in place",
    "Use dedicated obstacle recovery states with exactly one controllable action each",
    "Prefer short directed turns for side/front obstacles; use move_backward rarely and only after front blockage",
    "Reserve full_rotate for a dedicated stuck/last_resort path reached only after repeated front-obstacle failures"
  ],
